#: build-src/contrib.md:1
msgid "Contributing to numahop."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:3
msgid ""
"If you plan to contribute to numahop you might want to read the [coding "
"guidelines](https://github.com/NumaHOP/NumaHOP/)."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:5
msgid "Developpement environement."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:7
msgid ""
"The easiest way to test developpements locally is to use the dockerised "
"version."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:9
msgid ""
"The makefile makes management of the developpement loop rather easy. You can "
"see the full list of rules provided by the Makefile by running `make list`. "
"If you chose to use the docker you should run `make setup-docker` before "
"running `make build-docker`."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:13
msgid "You can see the NumaHOP logs with `make app-logs`."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:15
msgid ""
"Also the formating of both the front-end and backend is handled in the "
"makefile with `make fmt`."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:17
msgid ""
"The lifecycle of the composition is manage with `app-<action>` and "
"`env-<action>` rules. The actions provided by the makefile are:"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:19
msgid "up: Start all containers and start their services."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:20
msgid "stop: Stop the services keeping the containers up."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:21
msgid "down: Stop the containers."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:22
msgid "clean: Same as down detaching the volumes allowing for their deletion."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:24
msgid ""
"The makefile also provides ways to manage the mounted volumes in the docker "
"images. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:26
msgid "to reset the db you can run `make reset-db`."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/contrib.md:27
msgid ""
"to get a clean reinstall of Numahop `make reset-all`. Note the volumes can "
"only be reset by unmouting them from the containers."
msgstr ""

